  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "Two Samplers say one line every two bars: \"Hello. I am Soba. I sing in sines.\" The first voice is Chris, who made Soba. The second was made by a formant synthesizer, from pulses and noise. This Mixer's mutes pick which one the Vocoder hears: unmute **2** and mute **1** to hear a robot say it.",
      "position": [
        580.0,
        542.0
      ],
      "width": 300.0
    },
    {
      "text": "**Your own voice:** pick your mic under **Input**. Press **Rec** on the top Sampler, then say the line: the take starts on your first word, and the Sampler says it every two bars from then on (**Ctrl+Z** brings Chris back). Or mute **1** and unmute **3** on the voice Mixer to be heard live. Use headphones, so the mic doesn't hear the speakers.",
      "position": [
        270.0,
        2082.0
      ],
      "width": 290.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The same pad plays twice: bright and raw into the Vocoder's **Carrier**, and filtered dark underneath, so the chords carry on between the words.",
      "position": [
        40.0,
        3030.0
      ],
      "width": 380.0
    }
  ]
}